{
  "description": "Non-DataFrame coverage gaps across 4 categories totaling ~11,500 missing\nstatements. These are higher ROI than DataFrame queries because they protect\nthe core product (runners, generators, registry), CLI user experience, and\nplatform adapters.\n\nCategory breakdown (excluding DataFrame subsystem):\n- Core logic: ~12,629 miss at 76.5% (runners, generators, base adapter, ETL)\n- CLI: 3,123 miss at 70.6% (commands, config, output)\n- Cloud platforms: 7,409 miss at 59.4% (SQL generation, credentials)\n- Local platforms: 618 miss at 69.1% (DuckDB, DataFusion, Polars SQL)\n- Utils: 991 miss at 79.1% (validation, compilation, execution)\n\nTarget: ~9,500 additional statements covered, bringing non-DF code from\n~72% to ~82%. Combined with DataFrame TODO and coverage scope changes,\nthis reaches the 80% overall target.\n\nNote: TPC-DI ETL (transformations.py 1,053 miss + batch.py 882 miss = 1,935\nstmts) is deferred due to high effort and niche usage. This caps core_logic\nat ~79% even if all other core files hit 85%. The overall 80% target is still\nachievable because other categories (utils, local platforms) will exceed 85%.\n\nAll core/local/utils work is testable with real engines (DuckDB, DataFusion).\nCLI is testable via Click CliRunner. Cloud platforms test SQL generation and\nconfig logic without credentials.",
